Here are two polished options depending on your intended context:

### Option 1: Patent/Legal-Technical Style (Recommended)
*This version retains formal patent terminology (e.g., "said") while fixing grammatical errors, improving parallel structure, and enhancing overall readability.*

> An exemplary embodiment of the invention relates to a method for determining the hydraulic permeability of rocks within a subsurface region, the method comprising: 
> * measuring in situ, calculating, or both, at least one independent seismic velocity of rocks at different locations within said subsurface region;
> * determining at least one lithological unit in said subsurface region based on the measured seismic velocities;
> * acquiring, for the at least one lithological unit, at least one rock sample from at least one location within said subsurface region;
> * measuring the porosity and permeability of said rock sample as functions of stress;
> * measuring, calculating, or both, at least one independent seismic velocity of said at least one rock sample as a function of stress;
> * computing the stiff and compliant porosity of said at least one rock sample;
> * computing numerical coefficients of a given analytical permeability model based on the stiff and compliant porosities;
> * computing coefficients of a given analytical model of an elastic-compliance characteristic of the rock based on the stiff and compliant porosity;
> * computing the stiff and compliant porosity for a plurality of other locations within said subsurface region; and
> * computing the permeability of rocks belonging to said at least one lithological unit for both said at least one location and said plurality of other locations within said subsurface region.

---

### Option 2: Technical Paper / Journal Publication Style
*This version removes repetitive patent legalisms ("said", "at least one") where appropriate to provide a smoother, more elegant flow while preserving all original steps.*

> An exemplary embodiment of the invention relates to a method for determining the hydraulic permeability of rock formations within a subsurface region, comprising the following steps:
> 1. Measuring in situ, calculating, or both, independent seismic velocities of rocks across various locations in the subsurface region;
> 2. Identifying at least one lithological unit within the subsurface region based on the measured seismic velocities;
> 3. Acquiring one or more rock samples for the identified lithological unit from at least one location in the subsurface region;
> 4. Measuring the porosity and permeability of the rock sample as functions of stress;
> 5. Measuring, calculating, or both, independent seismic velocities of the rock sample as functions of stress;
> 6. Computing the stiff and compliant porosities of the rock sample;
> 7. Computing numerical coefficients of a specified analytical permeability model using the stiff and compliant porosities;
> 8. Computing coefficients of a specified analytical model representing the elastic-compliance characteristics of the rock based on the stiff and compliant porosities;
> 9. Computing the stiff and compliant porosities for a plurality of additional locations within the subsurface region; and
> 10. Computing the permeability of rocks within the identified lithological unit for both the primary location and the plurality of additional locations across the subsurface region.

---

### Key Improvements Made:
* **Grammar Corrections:** Fixed "relates a method" to "relates to a method", "an at least one" to "at least one", and removed the extraneous "of" in "calculating of at least one".
* **Parallel Structure:** Unified all procedural steps using clean, active verb forms (e.g., *measuring*, *determining*, *acquiring*, *computing*).
* **Clarity & Precision:** Changed "in-situ measuring" to "measuring in situ" and smoothed out the final clause ("for both said at least one location and said plurality of other locations").
